{"name":"Grime","hex":"#565143","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Grime","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Old Norse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Grime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dirt","blocks":[{"text":"Dirt  is any matter considered unclean, especially when in contact with a person's clothes, skin, or possessions. In such cases, they are said to become dirty.\nCommon types of dirt include:"},{"items":["Debris: scattered pieces of waste or remains","Dust: a general powder of organic or mineral matter","Filth: foul matter such as excrement","Grime: a black, ingrained dust such as soot","Soil: the mix of clay, sand, and humus which lies on top of bedrock. The term 'soil' may be used to refer to unwanted substances or dirt that are deposited onto surfaces such as clothing."]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/King%27s_Cross%2C_London%3B_the_Great_Dust-Heap%2C_next_to_Battle_Br_Wellcome_V0013642.jpg/330px-King%27s_Cross%2C_London%3B_the_Great_Dust-Heap%2C_next_to_Battle_Br_Wellcome_V0013642.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirt","wikidata":"Q112075129"},{"title":"Grime music","blocks":[{"text":"Grime is a genre of electronic dance music (EDM) that emerged in London in the early 2000s. It developed out of the earlier UK dance style UK garage, and draws influences from jungle, dancehall, and hip-hop. The style is typified by rapid, syncopated breakbeats, generally around 140 beats per minute, and often features an aggressive or jagged electronic sound. Emceeing is a significant element of the style, and lyrics often revolve around gritty depictions of urban life."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Grime_-_Roll_Deep_Crew.png/330px-Grime_-_Roll_Deep_Crew.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grime_music","wikidata":"Q1166726"},{"title":"Grime (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Grime is a 2021 Metroidvania video game developed by Israeli independent developer Clover Bite and published by Akupara Games. The game was released on August 2, 2021 for Windows and Google Stadia, followed by versions for PlayStation 4, PlayStation 5, Xbox One and Xbox Series X/S in December 2022, and a Nintendo Switch version in January 2024. It received generally positive reviews from critics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f4/Grime_%28video_game%29_logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grime_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q107860985"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Dirty_Dick%27s_-_geograph.org.uk_-_821364.jpg/330px-Dirty_Dick%27s_-_geograph.org.uk_-_821364.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Dirty_Dick%27s_-_geograph.org.uk_-_821364.jpg/330px-Dirty_Dick%27s_-_geograph.org.uk_-_821364.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dirty Dicks is a Bishopsgate pub named after Dirty Dick, who once owned it and was notoriously filthy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADirty_Dick's_-_geograph.org.uk_-_821364.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg/500px-Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg/1280px-Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg/500px-Sure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dirt-covered sidewalk in Brooklyn, NYC being swept during a community clean-up","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASure_We_Can_Earthday_clean_2021_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/RollDeep.jpg/500px-RollDeep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/RollDeep.jpg/500px-RollDeep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roll Deep, a well-known grime crew, performs at the 2006 Love Music Hate Racism festival.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARollDeep.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Dizzee_Rascal_2013.jpg/500px-Dizzee_Rascal_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Dizzee_Rascal_2013.jpg/500px-Dizzee_Rascal_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dizzee Rascal performing in 2013","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADizzee_Rascal_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/Grime_Boss_Battle_Screenshot_Windows.png/330px-Grime_Boss_Battle_Screenshot_Windows.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/Grime_Boss_Battle_Screenshot_Windows.png/330px-Grime_Boss_Battle_Screenshot_Windows.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Vessel landing a hit on one of the game's bosses for 66 damage - The Vessel's four essential metrics are located in the top left of the image and its mass on the bottom right.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrime_Boss_Battle_Screenshot_Windows.png"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"